/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Numbers chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("numbers", [
{n:6, name:"The Nazirite Vow", seal:{ref:"Numbers 6:24",verse:"The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:"}, facts:["Did you know the Nazirite vow could be taken by any man or woman, not just priests, making it one of Scripture's great callings open to ordinary people (Numbers 6:2)?","Did you know the Nazirite's uncut hair was called his consecration, a visible sign of a life set apart for God (Numbers 6:5-7)?","Did you know the priestly blessing of Numbers 6:24-26 is still spoken over children in Jewish homes every week, one of the oldest blessings in continuous use?"], questions:[
{q:"Who could take the vow of a Nazarite?", options:["Any man or woman who vowed to separate themselves unto the LORD","Only the sons of Aaron","Only the Levites","Only the elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:2",verse:"Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When either man or woman shall separate themselves to vow a vow of a Nazarite, to separate themselves unto the LORD:", insight:"Separation unto the LORD was open to any man or woman; consecration is not reserved for the clergy."},
{q:"From what drink did the Nazirite separate himself?", options:["Wine and strong drink","Milk and water","Only new wine","Only drink at feasts"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:3",verse:"He shall separate himself from wine and strong drink, and shall drink no vinegar of wine, or vinegar of strong drink, neither shall he drink any liquor of grapes, nor eat moist grapes, or dried.", insight:"He gave up even the vinegar of wine; consecration watches the small doors, not only the great ones."},
{q:"What of the vine was forbidden the Nazirite?", options:["Nothing made of the vine tree, from the kernels even to the husk","Only the wine, but grapes were allowed","Only strong drink","Only the dried raisins"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:4",verse:"All the days of his separation shall he eat nothing that is made of the vine tree, from the kernels even to the husk.", insight:"From kernel to husk, nothing of the vine; holiness does not bargain over the edges."},
{q:"What must never come upon the Nazirite's head?", options:["A razor","A crown of gold","A linen cap","Oil of anointing"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:5",verse:"All the days of the vow of his separation there shall no razor come upon his head: until the days be fulfilled, in the which he separateth himself unto the LORD, he shall be holy, and shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow.", insight:"No razor touched his head; his difference from other men was worn where all could see it."},
{q:"How long were the locks of his head to grow?", options:["All the days of his separation","Until the next new moon","For seven years","Until the year of jubilee"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:5",verse:"All the days of the vow of his separation there shall no razor come upon his head: until the days be fulfilled, in the which he separateth himself unto the LORD, he shall be holy, and shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow.", insight:"The growing hair marked time with God; consecration is measured in days, not moments."},
{q:"What contact was forbidden the Nazirite all his days?", options:["Coming near any dead body","Touching an unclean animal","Entering a stranger's house","Handling money"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:6",verse:"All the days that he separateth himself unto the LORD he shall come at no dead body.", insight:"Even the dead were kept at a distance; some separations guard the life God has set apart."},
{q:"For which relatives could he not be made unclean?", options:["His father, mother, brother, and sister","His wife and children","His uncle and aunt","His servants"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:7",verse:"He shall not make himself unclean for his father, or for his mother, for his brother, or for his sister, when they die: because the consecration of his God is upon his head.", insight:"Not even for father or mother; devotion to God outranks the dearest earthly ties."},
{q:"Why could he not defile himself for his kindred?", options:["The consecration of his God was upon his head","The priest had forbidden it","The camp was unclean","His vow had expired"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:7",verse:"He shall not make himself unclean for his father, or for his mother, for his brother, or for his sister, when they die: because the consecration of his God is upon his head.", insight:"The consecration of his God was upon his head; what God has crowned, even grief must not disturb."},
{q:"What happened if any man died very suddenly by him?", options:["He defiled the head of his consecration","His vow was doubled","He was cut off from Israel","He became a priest"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:9",verse:"And if any man die very suddenly by him, and he hath defiled the head of his consecration; then he shall shave his head in the day of his cleansing, on the seventh day shall he shave it.", insight:"Sudden, unplanned defilement still defiled; holiness is not kept by intentions alone."},
{q:"On what day did he shave his head after defilement?", options:["The seventh day, the day of his cleansing","The third day","The eighth day","The new moon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:9",verse:"And if any man die very suddenly by him, and he hath defiled the head of his consecration; then he shall shave his head in the day of his cleansing, on the seventh day shall he shave it.", insight:"Shaving marked a fresh start; God gives the defiled a set day to begin again."},
{q:"What did he bring the priest on the eighth day?", options:["Two turtles, or two young pigeons","A lamb and a ram","A basket of bread","A bottle of oil"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:10",verse:"And on the eighth day he shall bring two turtles, or two young pigeons, to the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:", insight:"Two small birds for a broken vow; God accepts the humble offering of the repentant."},
{q:"What did the priest offer the two birds for?", options:["The one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering","Both for peace offerings","Both for trespass offerings","One for the priest, one for the Nazirite"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:11",verse:"And the priest shall offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, and make an atonement for him, for that he sinned by the dead, and shall hallow his head that same day.", insight:"Sin offering and burnt offering together; atonement must come before the vow can be renewed."},
{q:"What trespass offering did he bring?", options:["A lamb of the first year","A bullock of two years","A goat of the flock","A turtle dove"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:12",verse:"And he shall consecrate unto the LORD the days of his separation, and shall bring a lamb of the first year for a trespass offering: but the days that were before shall be lost, because his separation was defiled.", insight:"A lamb for the trespass; even unintentional failure has a price, and God provides it."},
{q:"What became of the days of his vow before the defilement?", options:["They were lost","They were doubled","They were counted half","They were forgiven but kept"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:12",verse:"And he shall consecrate unto the LORD the days of his separation, and shall bring a lamb of the first year for a trespass offering: but the days that were before shall be lost, because his separation was defiled.", insight:"The former days were lost; consecration cannot be patched, it must be begun anew."},
{q:"What three animals were offered when the vow was fulfilled?", options:["A he lamb for a burnt offering, a ewe lamb for a sin offering, and a ram for peace offerings","Three bullocks","Three rams","A lamb, a goat, and a dove"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:14",verse:"And he shall offer his offering unto the LORD, one he lamb of the first year without blemish for a burnt offering, and one ewe lamb of the first year without blemish for a sin offering, and one ram without blemish for peace offerings,", insight:"Burnt, sin, and peace offerings; a finished vow ends in full surrender, cleansing, and fellowship."},
{q:"What was carried in the basket with the sacrifices?", options:["Unleavened bread, cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, and wafers anointed with oil","Leavened loaves and honey cakes","Parched corn and raisins","Manna and quails"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:15",verse:"And a basket of unleavened bread, cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, and wafers of unleavened bread anointed with oil, and their meat offering, and their drink offerings.", insight:"Unleavened bread with the sacrifices; sincerity without the leaven of pretense belongs at the altar."},
{q:"Where did the Nazirite shave the head of his separation?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle of the congregation","At the gate of the camp","On the mountain","By the river"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:18",verse:"And the Nazarite shall shave the head of his separation at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall take the hair of the head of his separation, and put it in the fire which is under the sacrifice of the peace offerings.", insight:"At the door of the tabernacle; the vow that began in private ended in public worship."},
{q:"Where did he put the hair of his separation?", options:["In the fire under the sacrifice of the peace offerings","In a chest in the sanctuary","He buried it outside the camp","He gave it to the priest"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:18",verse:"And the Nazarite shall shave the head of his separation at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall take the hair of the head of his separation, and put it in the fire which is under the sacrifice of the peace offerings.", insight:"The hair, the mark of his consecration, was burned with the peace offering; all we are goes on the altar."},
{q:"What is the second line of the priestly blessing?", options:["The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee","The LORD give thee gold and silver","The LORD make thee a prince among thy people","The LORD keep thee from all war"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:25",verse:"The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee:", insight:"His face shining upon you; the greatest blessing is not what God gives, but God Himself turned toward you."},
{q:"How does the priestly blessing end?", options:["The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace","The LORD make thee head and not the tail","The LORD bless thy land forever","The LORD establish thy throne"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 6:26",verse:"The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.", insight:"It ends with peace; every blessing of God aims at settling your heart in Him."}
]},
{n:7, name:"Offerings of the Princes", seal:{ref:"Numbers 7:89",verse:"And when Moses was gone into the tabernacle of the congregation to speak with him, then he heard the voice of one speaking unto him from off the mercy seat that was upon the ark of testimony, from between the two cherubims: and he spake unto him."}, facts:["Did you know every prince brought the exact same offering, so no tribe could out-give another before the altar (Numbers 7:12-83)?","Did you know the twelve days of dedication gifts came to 2,400 shekels of silver and 120 shekels of gold, besides all the herds (Numbers 7:85-86)?","Did you know the chapter ends with Moses hearing God's voice speaking from between the two cherubims on the mercy seat (Numbers 7:89)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did the princes of Israel offer when the tabernacle was set up?", options:["Six covered wagons and twelve oxen","Twelve horses and chariots","A chest of gold and silver","Seven rams for each tribe"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:3",verse:"And they brought their offering before the LORD, six covered wagons, and twelve oxen; a wagon for two of the princes, and for each one an ox: and they brought them before the tabernacle.", insight:"Wagons and oxen for the work; the leaders gave what the service actually needed."},
{q:"How were the wagons and oxen divided among the princes?", options:["Two princes brought one wagon, and each one an ox","Each prince brought a wagon and two oxen","The eldest prince gave all","They were divided by lot"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:3",verse:"And they brought their offering before the LORD, six covered wagons, and twelve oxen; a wagon for two of the princes, and for each one an ox: and they brought them before the tabernacle.", insight:"Each shared the load equally; no tribe carried the tabernacle alone."},
{q:"To whom did Moses give the wagons and oxen?", options:["Unto the Levites","Unto the priests","Unto the princes","Unto the elders"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:6",verse:"And Moses took the wagons and the oxen, and gave them unto the Levites.", insight:"Given to the Levites; gifts for God's house belong to those who do God's work."},
{q:"What did the sons of Gershon receive?", options:["Two wagons and four oxen","Four wagons and eight oxen","Six wagons and no oxen","One wagon and two oxen"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:7",verse:"Two wagons and four oxen he gave unto the sons of Gershon, according to their service:", insight:"Each family received according to its service; God equips according to the burden He assigns."},
{q:"What did the sons of Merari receive?", options:["Four wagons and eight oxen","Two wagons and four oxen","No wagons, only oxen","All the remaining wagons"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:8",verse:"And four wagons and eight oxen he gave unto the sons of Merari, according unto their service, under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.", insight:"Merari bore the heavy boards and needed the most help; God matches provision to the weight."},
{q:"Why did the sons of Kohath receive no wagons?", options:["Because the service of the sanctuary belonged unto them on their shoulders","Because they were the youngest","Because they had refused the gift","Because the princes forgot them"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:9",verse:"But unto the sons of Kohath he gave none: because the service of the sanctuary belonging unto them was that they should bear upon their shoulders.", insight:"The holy things rode on shoulders, not wagons; some service must be borne by hand, not by convenience."},
{q:"Who offered on the first day of the dedication?", options:["Nahshon the son of Amminadab, prince of Judah","Nethaneel the son of Zuar","Eliab the son of Helon","Elizur the son of Shedeur"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:12",verse:"And he that offered his offering the first day was Nahshon the son of Amminadab, of the tribe of Judah:", insight:"Judah led the giving, as Judah would lead the march; the tribe of praise goes first."},
{q:"Who offered on the second day?", options:["Nethaneel the son of Zuar, prince of Issachar","Nahshon the son of Amminadab","Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai","Ahira the son of Enan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:18",verse:"On the second day Nethaneel the son of Zuar, prince of Issachar, did offer:", insight:"Day by day, tribe by tribe; God gave each prince his own day before the altar."},
{q:"Who offered on the third day?", options:["Eliab the son of Helon, prince of Zebulun","Elishama the son of Ammihud","Abidan the son of Gideoni","Pagiel the son of Ocran"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:24",verse:"On the third day Eliab the son of Helon, prince of the children of Zebulun, did offer:", insight:"Twelve days, twelve princes; dedication is not hurried, and no one is overlooked."},
{q:"Which prince offered on the fourth day?", options:["Elizur the son of Shedeur, prince of Reuben","Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur","Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai","Eliasaph the son of Deuel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:30",verse:"On the fourth day Elizur the son of Shedeur, prince of the children of Reuben, did offer:", insight:"Reuben, the firstborn tribe, offered on the fourth day; place in line is God's to order."},
{q:"Which prince offered on the sixth day?", options:["Eliasaph the son of Deuel, prince of Gad","Elishama the son of Ammihud","Nethaneel the son of Zuar","Ahira the son of Enan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:42",verse:"On the sixth day Eliasaph the son of Deuel, prince of the children of Gad, offered:", insight:"Every prince named, every day counted; God records the givers, not just the gifts."},
{q:"Which prince offered on the seventh day?", options:["Elishama the son of Ammihud, prince of Ephraim","Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur","Abidan the son of Gideoni","Pagiel the son of Ocran"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:48",verse:"On the seventh day Elishama the son of Ammihud, prince of the children of Ephraim, offered:", insight:"Ephraim's prince gave the same as all the rest; before the altar, tribes stand equal."},
{q:"Who offered on the twelfth and final day?", options:["Ahira the son of Enan, prince of Naphtali","Pagiel the son of Ocran","Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai","Nahshon the son of Amminadab"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:78",verse:"On the twelfth day Ahira the son of Enan, prince of the children of Naphtali, offered:", insight:"Naphtali closed the twelve days; the last giver is as honored as the first."},
{q:"What silver vessels did each prince bring?", options:["A silver charger of a hundred and thirty shekels, and a silver bowl of seventy shekels","Two bowls of fifty shekels each","A charger of gold and a bowl of silver","Twelve spoons of silver"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:13",verse:"And his offering was one silver charger, the weight thereof was an hundred and thirty shekels, one silver bowl of seventy shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary; both of them were full of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering:", insight:"Both vessels were full of fine flour mingled with oil; giving to God is full measure, not the leftovers."},
{q:"With what was the golden spoon of ten shekels filled?", options:["Incense","Manna","Oil","Fine flour"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:14",verse:"One spoon of ten shekels of gold, full of incense:", insight:"A spoon of gold full of incense; the smallest vessel can carry the sweetest offering."},
{q:"What did all twelve golden spoons weigh together?", options:["An hundred and twenty shekels","Two hundred and forty shekels","Sixty shekels","Twelve shekels"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:86",verse:"The golden spoons were twelve, full of incense, weighing ten shekels apiece, after the shekel of the sanctuary: all the gold of the spoons was an hundred and twenty shekels.", insight:"Twelve spoons, one hundred and twenty shekels; God weighs what we give, and He remembers the total."},
{q:"What did each prince bring for a burnt offering?", options:["One young bullock, one ram, one lamb of the first year","Two bullocks and a ram","A lamb only","Seven doves"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:15",verse:"One young bullock, one ram, one lamb of the first year, for a burnt offering:", insight:"Bullock, ram, and lamb; the burnt offering was wholly consumed, a picture of total surrender."},
{q:"What did each prince bring for a sin offering?", options:["One kid of the goats","A red heifer","Two turtle doves","A ewe lamb"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:16",verse:"One kid of the goats for a sin offering:", insight:"One kid of the goats for sin; even at a dedication feast, atonement comes first."},
{q:"What did each prince bring for peace offerings?", options:["Two oxen, five rams, five he goats, five lambs of the first year","One ox and two rams","Seven lambs","A bullock and a goat"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:17",verse:"And for a sacrifice of peace offerings, two oxen, five rams, five he goats, five lambs of the first year: this was the offering of Nahshon the son of Amminadab.", insight:"The peace offering fed the people; dedication ended in fellowship around God's table."},
{q:"What did Moses hear when he entered the tabernacle?", options:["The voice of one speaking unto him from off the mercy seat, from between the two cherubims","Thunder from the mount","A choir of angels","The sound of the trumpets"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 7:89",verse:"And when Moses was gone into the tabernacle of the congregation to speak with him, then he heard the voice of one speaking unto him from off the mercy seat that was upon the ark of testimony, from between the two cherubims: and he spake unto him.", insight:"God spoke from between the cherubims; after the giving came the voice, for He meets those who honor Him."}
]},
{n:8, name:"The Cleansing of the Levites", seal:{ref:"Numbers 8:14",verse:"Thus shalt thou separate the Levites from among the children of Israel: and the Levites shall be mine."}, facts:["Did you know the Levites were taken in place of every firstborn son of Israel, whom God had claimed when He struck Egypt (Numbers 8:16-17)?","Did you know Levites began tabernacle service at twenty-five but stepped back from the heavy labor at fifty, while still helping their brothers (Numbers 8:24-26)?","Did you know all Israel laid hands on the Levites as they were presented, showing the whole people gave them to God's work (Numbers 8:10)?"], questions:[
{q:"What was Aaron to do with the seven lamps?", options:["Light them so they give light over against the candlestick","Put them out at evening","Carry them outside the camp","Melt them down for gold"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:2",verse:"Speak unto Aaron, and say unto him, When thou lightest the lamps, the seven lamps shall give light over against the candlestick.", insight:"The lamps shone toward the candlestick; ministry is light directed at God's presence, not at men."},
{q:"How was the candlestick made?", options:["Of beaten work of gold","Of cast silver","Of wood overlaid with brass","Of hammered iron"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:4",verse:"And this work of the candlestick was of beaten gold, unto the shaft thereof, unto the flowers thereof, was beaten work: according unto the pattern which the LORD had shewed Moses, so he made the candlestick.", insight:"Beaten work of gold; the vessel of light was shaped by hammering, as servants are shaped by trials."},
{q:"With what water were the Levites sprinkled?", options:["The water of purifying","The water of the laver","Water from the Jordan","Rain water"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:7",verse:"And thus shalt thou do unto them, to cleanse them: Sprinkle water of purifying upon them, and let them shave all their flesh, and let them wash their clothes, and so make themselves clean.", insight:"The water of purifying; those who serve holy things must first be made clean."},
{q:"What were the Levites to do with all their flesh?", options:["Shave it all","Anoint it with oil","Cover it with sackcloth","Wash it seven times"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:7",verse:"And thus shalt thou do unto them, to cleanse them: Sprinkle water of purifying upon them, and let them shave all their flesh, and let them wash their clothes, and so make themselves clean.", insight:"They shaved all their flesh; consecration strips away the old before putting on the new."},
{q:"What did the LORD first command Moses to do with the Levites?", options:["Take the Levites from among the children of Israel, and cleanse them","Number them with the firstborn","Send them outside the camp","Anoint them with oil"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:6",verse:"Take the Levites from among the children of Israel, and cleanse them.", insight:"'Take... and cleanse them'; God's first move with His servants is always cleansing."},
{q:"What two bullocks were taken for the Levites?", options:["One young bullock with a meat offering for a burnt offering, and another for a sin offering","Two bullocks for peace offerings","A bullock and a ram","Two red heifers"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:8",verse:"Then let them take a young bullock with his meat offering, even fine flour mingled with oil, and another young bullock shalt thou take for a sin offering.", insight:"Burnt offering and sin offering; those set apart for God begin with atonement and surrender."},
{q:"Who laid their hands upon the Levites?", options:["The children of Israel","Aaron alone","Moses alone","The princes only"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:10",verse:"And thou shalt bring the Levites before the LORD: and the children of Israel shall put their hands upon the Levites:", insight:"All Israel laid hands on them; the Levites belonged to the whole people, given back to God."},
{q:"What did Aaron do with the Levites before the LORD?", options:["Offered them for an offering waved before the LORD","Anointed them with oil","Clothed them in blue","Set them outside the camp"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:11",verse:"And Aaron shall offer the Levites before the LORD for an offering of the children of Israel, that they may execute the service of the LORD.", insight:"Aaron waved them as an offering; the Levites themselves were the gift laid on God's altar."},
{q:"Whose hands were laid on the heads of the bullocks?", options:["The Levites' hands","Aaron's hands","Moses' hands","The elders' hands"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:12",verse:"And the Levites shall lay their hands upon the heads of the bullocks: and thou shalt offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, unto the LORD, to make an atonement for the Levites.", insight:"The Levites laid hands on the bullocks; even the consecrated need a sacrifice for themselves."},
{q:"What were the two bullocks offered for?", options:["The one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering","Both for peace offerings","Both for trespass offerings","One for each family of Levi"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:12",verse:"And the Levites shall lay their hands upon the heads of the bullocks: and thou shalt offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, unto the LORD, to make an atonement for the Levites.", insight:"Sin offering first, then burnt; cleansing precedes consecration in God's order."},
{q:"How were the Levites separated from Israel?", options:["Set apart from among the children of Israel, to be the LORD's","Sent to live outside the camp","Numbered with the firstborn","Joined to the priests by marriage"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:14",verse:"Thus shalt thou separate the Levites from among the children of Israel: and the Levites shall be mine.", insight:"'The Levites shall be mine'; separation is not rejection, it is belonging to God in a special way."},
{q:"In whose place did God take the Levites?", options:["Instead of all the firstborn that open the matrix among the children of Israel","Instead of the elders","Instead of the soldiers","Instead of the princes"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:16",verse:"For they are wholly given unto me from among the children of Israel; instead of such as open every womb, even instead of the firstborn of all the children of Israel, have I taken them unto me.", insight:"Taken instead of the firstborn; God claimed a tribe to stand where every family's eldest should have stood."},
{q:"Why had God claimed all the firstborn of Israel?", options:["Because He smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt","Because they were the strongest","Because the law required it","Because Israel had promised it"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:17",verse:"For all the firstborn of the children of Israel are mine, both man and beast: on the day that I smote every firstborn in the land of Egypt I sanctified them for myself.", insight:"The night He struck Egypt, He claimed Israel's firstborn; redemption always creates a debt of belonging."},
{q:"To whom did God give the Levites as a gift?", options:["To Aaron and to his sons","To Moses","To the princes of Israel","To the elders of the congregation"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:19",verse:"And I have given the Levites as a gift to Aaron and to his sons from among the children of Israel, to do the service of the children of Israel in the tabernacle of the congregation, and to make an atonement for the children of Israel: that there be no plague among the children of Israel, when the children of Israel come nigh unto the sanctuary.", insight:"A gift to Aaron and his sons; God provides helpers for those who bear the heaviest callings."},
{q:"Why were the Levites given to Aaron?", options:["To do the service of the tabernacle and make atonement, that there be no plague","To carry the ark into battle","To judge the people","To keep the records of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:19",verse:"And I have given the Levites as a gift to Aaron and to his sons from among the children of Israel, to do the service of the children of Israel in the tabernacle of the congregation, and to make an atonement for the children of Israel: that there be no plague among the children of Israel, when the children of Israel come nigh unto the sanctuary.", insight:"To serve and to make atonement; ministry shields the people from the plague of approaching God unprepared."},
{q:"What did the Levites do before entering the service?", options:["Purified themselves and washed their clothes","Fasted forty days","Built new tents","Offered a ram each"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:21",verse:"And the Levites were purified, and they washed their clothes; and Aaron offered them as an offering before the LORD; and Aaron made an atonement for them to cleanse them.", insight:"Purified and washed; no one enters God's service on yesterday's cleanness."},
{q:"What did Aaron do for the Levites?", options:["Offered them as an offering waved before the LORD and made an atonement for them","Crowned them with gold","Gave them cities to dwell in","Sent them to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:21",verse:"And the Levites were purified, and they washed their clothes; and Aaron offered them as an offering before the LORD; and Aaron made an atonement for them to cleanse them.", insight:"Aaron made atonement for them; even God's chosen servants are covered by another's offering."},
{q:"At what age did a Levite enter the service of the tabernacle?", options:["From twenty and five years old and upward","From twenty years old","From thirty years old","From eighteen years old"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:24",verse:"This is it that belongeth unto the Levites: from twenty and five years old and upward they shall go in to wait upon the service of the tabernacle of the congregation:", insight:"Twenty-five years; God waits for maturity before laying His work on young shoulders."},
{q:"At what age did the Levite cease waiting upon the service?", options:["From fifty years old","From sixty years old","From forty years old","He served until death"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:25",verse:"And from the age of fifty years they shall cease waiting upon the service thereof, and shall serve no more:", insight:"At fifty he stepped back from the labor; God honors the aging servant with rest, not rejection."},
{q:"What could the older Levites still do?", options:["Minister with their brethren in the tabernacle and keep the charge, but do no service","Teach the law in the cities","Offer sacrifices","Lead the armies"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 8:26",verse:"But shall minister with their brethren in the tabernacle of the congregation, to keep the charge, and shall do no service. Thus shalt thou do unto the Levites touching their charge.", insight:"They kept the charge but did no service; age changes the work, not the worth, of God's servant."}
]},
{n:9, name:"The Second Passover", seal:{ref:"Numbers 9:23",verse:"At the commandment of the LORD they rested in the tents, and at the commandment of the LORD they journeyed: they kept the charge of the LORD, at the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses."}, facts:["Did you know the second Passover let the unclean and the traveler keep the feast a month late, so no one missed God's appointed mercy (Numbers 9:10-11)?","Did you know the same law of Passover bound the stranger and the homeborn alike, one ordinance for all (Numbers 9:14)?","Did you know Israel moved only when the cloud moved, whether it tarried two days, a month, or a year, marching by God's signal alone (Numbers 9:22)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did the LORD command the second Passover?", options:["In the first month of the second year after they came out of Egypt","In the third year in Canaan","In the fortieth year","In the first month of the first year"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:1",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the first month of the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt, saying,", insight:"A year after the exodus, still in the wilderness; God keeps His feasts even before His people reach the promise."},
{q:"What were the children of Israel to keep?", options:["The passover at his appointed season","The feast of trumpets","The year of jubilee","A new moon festival"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:2",verse:"Let the children of Israel also keep the passover at his appointed season.", insight:"'At his appointed season'; God's calendar does not bend to our convenience."},
{q:"On what day of the month was it kept?", options:["The fourteenth day of the month, at even","The first day","The tenth day","The twenty-first day"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:3",verse:"In the fourteenth day of this month, at even, ye shall keep it in his appointed season: according to all the rites of it, and according to all the ceremonies thereof, shall ye keep it.", insight:"The fourteenth day at even, as in Egypt; God keeps His appointments to the very day."},
{q:"According to what were they to keep it?", options:["According to all the rites and ceremonies thereof","According to the custom of Egypt","As each family pleased","According to the new law of the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:3",verse:"In the fourteenth day of this month, at even, ye shall keep it in his appointed season: according to all the rites of it, and according to all the ceremonies thereof, shall ye keep it.", insight:"All the rites and ceremonies; worship is not improved by our edits."},
{q:"Where did they keep the Passover?", options:["In the wilderness of Sinai","In the land of Goshen","At the Red Sea","In the plains of Moab"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:5",verse:"And they kept the passover on the fourteenth day of the first month at even in the wilderness of Sinai: according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did the children of Israel.", insight:"In the wilderness of Sinai; redemption is remembered even in the middle of the journey."},
{q:"Why were certain men defiled?", options:["By the dead body of a man","By touching a leper","By eating unclean food","By entering a tomb"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:6",verse:"And there were certain men, who were defiled by the dead body of a man, that they could not keep the passover on that day: and they came before Moses and before Aaron on that day:", insight:"Defiled by the dead; their grief over a burial had kept them from the feast, and they mourned the loss."},
{q:"What did the defiled men ask Moses?", options:["Wherefore are we kept back, that we may not offer an offering of the LORD?","When will the camp move?","Who shall bury our dead?","Are we cut off forever?"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:7",verse:"And those men said unto him, We are defiled by the dead body of a man: wherefore are we kept back, that we may not offer an offering of the LORD in his appointed season among the children of Israel?", insight:"They hungered to offer; a heart that grieves missing worship is a heart God will answer."},
{q:"What did Moses say to the defiled men?", options:["Stand still, and I will hear what the LORD will command concerning you","Go, and wash yourselves","Wait until next year","Offer without the lamb"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:8",verse:"And Moses said unto them, Stand still, and I will hear what the LORD will command concerning you.", insight:"'Stand still'; Moses did not guess at God's will, he waited to hear it."},
{q:"Who was allowed to keep the Passover in the second month?", options:["He that is unclean by a dead body, or in a journey afar off","Only the priests","Only the elders","Only the firstborn"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:10",verse:"Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If any man of you or of your posterity shall be unclean by reason of a dead body, or be in a journey afar off, yet he shall keep the passover unto the LORD.", insight:"The unclean and the traveler got a second month; God's mercy makes room for the hindered."},
{q:"When was the second Passover kept?", options:["The fourteenth day of the second month, at even","The first day of the second month","The fourteenth day of the third month","The last day of the year"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:11",verse:"The fourteenth day of the second month at even they shall keep it, and eat it with unleavened bread and bitter herbs.", insight:"A month later, but the same feast; grace gives a second date without lowering the standard."},
{q:"With what was the Passover lamb eaten?", options:["With unleavened bread and bitter herbs","With leavened bread and honey","With manna and quails","With wine and oil"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:11",verse:"The fourteenth day of the second month at even they shall keep it, and eat it with unleavened bread and bitter herbs.", insight:"Unleavened bread and bitter herbs; redemption is remembered with sincerity and with the taste of bondage."},
{q:"What were they commanded not to break?", options:["Not a bone of the lamb","The bread","The covenant","The fast"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:12",verse:"They shall leave none of it unto the morning, nor break any bone of it: according to all the ordinances of the passover they shall keep it.", insight:"Not a bone broken; the whole lamb pointed to the whole Christ, none of Him wasted or divided."},
{q:"How long could they leave the lamb?", options:["They were to leave none of it unto the morning","Until the third day","For seven days","Until the new moon"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:12",verse:"They shall leave none of it unto the morning, nor break any bone of it: according to all the ordinances of the passover they shall keep it.", insight:"None left till morning; God's provision is for the appointed night, not for hoarding."},
{q:"What happened to the clean man who neglected the Passover?", options:["He was cut off from among his people","He was fined a lamb","He was sent outside the camp for a week","He was beaten with stripes"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:13",verse:"But the man that is clean, and is not in a journey, and forbeareth to keep the passover, even the same soul shall be cut off from among his people: because he brought not the offering of the LORD in his appointed season, that man shall bear his sin.", insight:"Cut off for neglect; despising God's appointed mercy is as serious as breaking His law."},
{q:"What law covered the stranger who would keep the Passover?", options:["One ordinance for the stranger and for him that was born in the land","The stranger kept a different feast","The stranger was exempt","The stranger watched but did not eat"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:14",verse:"And if a stranger shall sojourn among you, and will keep the passover unto the LORD; according to the ordinance of the passover, and according to the manner thereof, so shall he do: ye shall have one ordinance, both for the stranger, and for him that was born in the land.", insight:"One ordinance for stranger and homeborn; God's table has one rule for all who come."},
{q:"What covered the tabernacle by day?", options:["The cloud","A linen veil","The smoke of the offerings","A pillar of salt"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:15",verse:"And on the day that the tabernacle was reared up the cloud covered the tabernacle, namely, the tent of the testimony: and at even there was upon the tabernacle as it were the appearance of fire, until the morning.", insight:"The cloud covered it by day; God's presence was Israel's shelter in the open wilderness."},
{q:"What appeared over the tabernacle by night?", options:["As it were the appearance of fire","A bright star","Lightning","A burning lamp"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:15",verse:"And on the day that the tabernacle was reared up the cloud covered the tabernacle, namely, the tent of the testimony: and at even there was upon the tabernacle as it were the appearance of fire, until the morning.", insight:"Fire by night; the same God who shades by day warms and guides in the dark."},
{q:"When did the children of Israel journey?", options:["When the cloud was taken up from the tabernacle","At every new moon","When Moses commanded","When the trumpets sounded"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:17",verse:"And when the cloud was taken up from the tabernacle, then after that the children of Israel journeyed: and in the place where the cloud abode, there the children of Israel pitched their tents.", insight:"They moved when the cloud moved; Israel's marches were set by heaven, not by impatience."},
{q:"How long did they abide when the cloud tarried?", options:["Whether two days, or a month, or a year, they journeyed not","Exactly forty days","Until the priests agreed","No longer than a week"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:22",verse:"Or whether it were two days, or a month, or a year, that the cloud tarried upon the tabernacle, remaining thereon, the children of Israel abode in their tents, and journeyed not: but when it was taken up, they journeyed.", insight:"Two days or a year, they stayed; waiting on God is as much obedience as marching."},
{q:"At whose commandment did they rest and journey?", options:["At the commandment of the LORD","At the commandment of Moses","At the commandment of the princes","At the commandment of Aaron"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 9:23",verse:"At the commandment of the LORD they rested in the tents, and at the commandment of the LORD they journeyed: they kept the charge of the LORD, at the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.", insight:"At the commandment of the LORD they rested and journeyed; every camp and every march was an act of worship."}
]},
{n:10, name:"The Silver Trumpets", seal:{ref:"Numbers 10:35",verse:"And it came to pass, when the ark set forward, that Moses said, Rise up, LORD, and let thine enemies be scattered; and let them that hate thee flee before thee."}, facts:["Did you know the two silver trumpets gave different signals: one blast summoned the leaders, two the whole assembly, and an alarm set the camps marching (Numbers 10:3-6)?","Did you know Judah marched first with Nahshon at its head, the tribe that would one day give Israel its kings (Numbers 10:14)?","Did you know Moses asked Hobab to come along because he knew the wilderness, to be 'instead of eyes' for Israel (Numbers 10:29-31)?"], questions:[
{q:"How many trumpets was Moses to make?", options:["Two trumpets","Seven trumpets","One trumpet","Twelve trumpets"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:2",verse:"Make thee two trumpets of silver; of a whole piece shalt thou make them: that thou mayest use them for the calling of the assembly, and for the journeying of the camps.", insight:"Two trumpets; God orders even the signals of His people with precision."},
{q:"Of what were the trumpets made?", options:["Of silver, of a whole piece","Of gold, beaten thin","Of brass from the laver","Of rams' horns"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:2",verse:"Make thee two trumpets of silver; of a whole piece shalt thou make them: that thou mayest use them for the calling of the assembly, and for the journeying of the camps.", insight:"Silver, of a whole piece; the call of God is pure metal, no joints, no mixture."},
{q:"How long was the blowing of the trumpets to be an ordinance?", options:["An ordinance for ever throughout their generations","Until Israel entered Canaan","For forty years only","Until the temple was built"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:8",verse:"And the sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow with the trumpets; and they shall be to you for an ordinance for ever throughout your generations.", insight:"'For ever throughout your generations'; the call of God does not expire with the wilderness."},
{q:"When both trumpets were blown, who gathered?", options:["All the assembly to the door of the tabernacle","The princes only","The Levites only","The army"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:3",verse:"And when they shall blow with them, all the assembly shall assemble themselves to thee at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.", insight:"Both trumpets, the whole assembly; when God calls everyone, no one is excused."},
{q:"When but one trumpet was blown, who gathered?", options:["The princes, the heads of the thousands of Israel","All the people","The women and children","The strangers"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:4",verse:"And if they blow but with one trumpet, then the princes, which are heads of the thousands of Israel, shall gather themselves unto thee.", insight:"One trumpet for the leaders; God speaks to the heads first, that they may lead the rest."},
{q:"What happened when the alarm was blown?", options:["The camps that lie on the east parts went forward","The people stood still","The priests entered the holy place","The cloud descended"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:5",verse:"When ye blow an alarm, then the camps that lie on the east parts shall go forward.", insight:"The east went forward first; at God's alarm, there is an order to the advance."},
{q:"What happened at the second alarm?", options:["The camps on the south side took their journey","The people returned to Egypt","The ark was covered","The trumpets were silent"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:6",verse:"When ye blow an alarm the second time, then the camps that lie on the south side shall take their journey: they shall blow an alarm for their journeys.", insight:"South at the second alarm; God moves His people in sequence, not in confusion."},
{q:"How was the congregation gathered without marching?", options:["They blew, but did not sound an alarm","They shouted with a great shout","The priests ran through the camp","The cloud flashed fire"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:7",verse:"But when the congregation is to be gathered together, ye shall blow, but ye shall not sound an alarm.", insight:"Blow, but no alarm; gathering for worship sounds different from marching to war."},
{q:"Who was to blow the trumpets?", options:["The sons of Aaron, the priests","The Levites","The princes","Moses himself"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:8",verse:"And the sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow with the trumpets; and they shall be to you for an ordinance for ever throughout your generations.", insight:"The priests blew them; the call of God comes through consecrated hands."},
{q:"What promise came with the alarm in time of war?", options:["Ye shall be remembered before the LORD your God, and saved from your enemies","Ye shall have double portions","Your enemies shall flee at the first sound","No battle shall be fought"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:9",verse:"And if ye go to war in your land against the enemy that oppresseth you, then ye shall blow an alarm with the trumpets; and ye shall be remembered before the LORD your God, and ye shall be saved from your enemies.", insight:"'Ye shall be remembered'; in the day of battle, God's memory is your shield."},
{q:"When else were the trumpets blown?", options:["In the day of gladness, in solemn days, and in the beginnings of months, over the offerings","Only at funerals","Only at the new year","When the king was born"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:10",verse:"Also in the day of your gladness, and in your solemn days, and in the beginnings of your months, ye shall blow with the trumpets over your burnt offerings, and over the sacrifices of your peace offerings; that they may be to you for a memorial before your God: I am the LORD your God.", insight:"Blown over the offerings in gladness; joy itself is to be sounded before God."},
{q:"On what day was the cloud taken up from the tabernacle?", options:["The twentieth day of the second month, in the second year","The first day of the first month","The fourteenth day of the first month","The tenth day of the seventh month"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:11",verse:"And it came to pass on the twentieth day of the second month, in the second year, that the cloud was taken up from off the tabernacle of the testimony.", insight:"The twentieth day of the second month; after a year at Sinai, the cloud moved and the nation marched."},
{q:"Which standard set forward first?", options:["The standard of the camp of the children of Judah","The standard of Reuben","The standard of Ephraim","The standard of Dan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:14",verse:"In the first place went the standard of the camp of the children of Judah according to their armies: and over his host was Nahshon the son of Amminadab.", insight:"Judah first; the tribe of praise leads the march, as praise should lead every advance."},
{q:"Who was over the host of Judah?", options:["Nahshon the son of Amminadab","Nethaneel the son of Zuar","Eliab the son of Helon","Elizur the son of Shedeur"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:14",verse:"In the first place went the standard of the camp of the children of Judah according to their armies: and over his host was Nahshon the son of Amminadab.", insight:"Nahshon led Judah; God puts named men at the head of His people's going."},
{q:"Who bore the sanctuary when the camp moved?", options:["The sons of Kohath","The sons of Gershon","The sons of Merari","The priests alone"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:21",verse:"And the Kohathites set forward, bearing the sanctuary: and the other did set up the tabernacle against they came.", insight:"The Kohathites bore the holy things on their shoulders; the weightiest service is carried, not carted."},
{q:"Which tribe formed the rereward of all the camps?", options:["The camp of the children of Dan","The camp of Naphtali","The camp of Asher","The camp of Benjamin"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:25",verse:"And the standard of the camp of the children of Dan set forward, which was the rereward of all the camps throughout their hosts: and over his host was Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.", insight:"Dan closed the march; God guards the rear of His people as surely as He leads the front."},
{q:"Whom did Moses ask to journey with Israel?", options:["Hobab, the son of Raguel the Midianite, Moses' father in law","Jethro himself","The king of Midian","The elders of Sinai"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:29",verse:"And Moses said unto Hobab, the son of Raguel the Midianite, Moses’ father in law, We are journeying unto the place of which the LORD said, I will give it you: come thou with us, and we will do thee good: for the LORD hath spoken good concerning Israel.", insight:"Moses invited his kinsman; the blessings of God are meant to be shared with family."},
{q:"What did Moses say Hobab would be to Israel?", options:["Instead of eyes","Instead of a guide for war","Instead of a priest","Instead of a judge"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:31",verse:"And he said, Leave us not, I pray thee; forasmuch as thou knowest how we are to encamp in the wilderness, and thou mayest be to us instead of eyes.", insight:"'Instead of eyes'; God uses a man's knowledge of the wilderness for the good of His people."},
{q:"How far did the ark go before the people?", options:["Three days' journey, to search out a resting place for them","One day's journey","Seven days' journey","To the borders of Canaan"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:33",verse:"And they departed from the mount of the LORD three days’ journey: and the ark of the covenant of the LORD went before them in the three days’ journey, to search out a resting place for them.", insight:"The ark went three days ahead; God's presence searches out our rest before we arrive."},
{q:"What did Moses say when the ark set forward?", options:["Rise up, LORD, and let thine enemies be scattered; and let them that hate thee flee before thee","Blessed be the LORD forever","The LORD is our banner","Go before us, O God of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Numbers 10:35",verse:"And it came to pass, when the ark set forward, that Moses said, Rise up, LORD, and let thine enemies be scattered; and let them that hate thee flee before thee.", insight:"'Rise up, LORD'; every advance of God's people begins with a prayer, not a plan."}
]}
]);
